{"_id":"10GYcyFobVS5uaP6","name":"Heritor","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"This is a class for a character with multiple sections to control multiple sections at the same time. Those who excel in this class are called Shapeshifters or Heritors.\nWhen you learn the Heritor class, characters with multiple sections can treat this class as the Standard Value when attempting some checks in actions outside the Main Section.\nCharacters without this class must make those checks as a straight roll (see CR I, p. 91).\nIn addition, you can learn special techniques called Infusions every time the Heritor class rises by 1 level.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:heritor","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Heritors learn one Infusion per Heritor Class level along with upgrading the basic values of each section of a character with multiple sections to the corresponding \"heritor level\"(see the table below).","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nThis is a class for a character with multiple sections to control multiple sections at the same time. Those who excel in this class are called Shapeshifters or Heritors.\nWhen you learn the Heritor class, characters with multiple sections can treat this class as the Standard Value when attempting some checks in actions outside the Main Section.\nCharacters without this class must make those checks as a straight roll (see CR I, p. 91).\nIn addition, you can learn special techniques called Infusions every time the Heritor class rises by 1 level.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nClass Features: Heritors learn one Infusion per Heritor Class level along with upgrading the basic values of each section of a character with multiple sections to the corresponding \"heritor level\"(see the table below).\nOther Requirements: While no race is prohibited from learning this class, only characters with multiple sections, such as Diablos, Drakes, Basilisks, and Scissorscorpions, gain any benefit from it.\nNote: Certain infusions are exclusive to Diablos, Drakes, Basilisks, or Scissorscorpions.\nCommon Infusions List\nBasilisks Infusions List\nDiablos Infusions List\nDrakes Infusions List\nScissorscorpions Infusions List\n\nBasic Values of Multiple Sections\n\nHeritor Level\nHead\nBody or Upper Body\nWing\nEvil Eye\nScorpion Tail\nPincers\n\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\nMax HP\nMax MP\nDef.\n\n0\n14\n10\n1\n20\n10\n1\n10\n5\n0\n10\n10\n0\n16\n6\n2\n12\n6\n2\n\n1\n17\n12\n1\n24\n12\n2\n13\n6\n1\n12\n12\n0\n20\n8\n3\n15\n8\n2\n\n2\n20\n14\n2\n28\n14\n3\n16\n7\n2\n14\n14\n0\n24\n10\n4\n18\n10\n3\n\n3\n23\n16\n2\n32\n16\n4\n19\n9\n3\n16\n16\n0\n28\n12\n5\n21\n12\n3\n\n4\n26\n18\n3\n36\n18\n5\n22\n11\n4\n18\n18\n1\n32\n14\n6\n24\n14\n4\n\n5\n29\n20\n3\n40\n20\n6\n25\n13\n5\n20\n20\n1\n37\n16\n7\n27\n16\n4\n\n6\n32\n22\n4\n44\n22\n7\n28\n15\n6\n22\n22\n1\n42\n18\n8\n31\n18\n5\n\n7\n36\n24\n4\n48\n25\n8\n32\n17\n7\n24\n24\n2\n47\n21\n9\n35\n20\n5\n\n8\n40\n26\n5\n53\n28\n9\n36\n19\n8\n27\n27\n2\n52\n24\n10\n39\n22\n6\n\n9\n44\n29\n5\n58\n31\n10\n40\n21\n9\n30\n30\n2\n58\n27\n11\n43\n24\n6\n\n10\n48\n32\n6\n63\n34\n11\n44\n23\n10\n33\n33\n3\n64\n30\n12\n47\n26\n7\n\n11\n52\n35\n7\n68\n37\n12\n48\n26\n11\n36\n36\n3\n70\n33\n13\n52\n28\n7\n\n12\n56\n38\n7\n73\n41\n13\n53\n29\n12\n39\n39\n3\n76\n36\n14\n57\n30\n8\n\n13\n60\n41\n8\n78\n45\n14\n58\n32\n13\n42\n42\n4\n83\n40\n15\n62\n32\n8\n\n14\n65\n44\n8\n83\n49\n15\n63\n35\n14\n45\n45\n4\n90\n44\n16\n67\n34\n9\n\n15\n70\n47\n9\n88\n53\n16\n68\n38\n15\n48\n48\n4\n97\n48\n17\n72\n36\n9\n\nSource: BR p. 57"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"1hSYmWpleRgJjJgX","name":"Conjurer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"This caster learns Spiritualism Magic. Spiritualism spells offer a variety of supportive effects, and the ability to manipulate constructs, such as dolls, for reconnaissance and other useful tasks.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:conjurer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Conjurers can cast any spell from the Spiritualism spells list of their Conjurer Class level or lower. Conjurers may also summon Golems and Undead. See CR II, p. 87 for more information.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThis caster learns Spiritualism Magic. Spiritualism spells offer a variety of supportive effects, and the ability to manipulate constructs, such as dolls, for reconnaissance and other useful tasks.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Spiritualism spells, a Conjurer must be able to vocalize, move their arms freely, and carry a magical implement. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Spiritualism Magic only)\nClass Features: Conjurers can cast any spell from the Spiritualism spells list of their Conjurer Class level or lower. Conjurers may also summon Golems and Undead. See CR II, p. 87 for more information.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Conjurers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Spiritualism), calculated as Conjurer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Conjurer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Conjurers learn to speak, read, and write the Arcana language, which they use to cast spells.\nSource: CR I, p. 88; CR II, p. 87; ET, p. 28; MA, p. 86\nSpiritualism Magic Spells List\nList of Golems\nList of Undead\nConjurer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"42G5LBjTQRkHqY6D","name":"Marksman","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"All ranged attacks (see CR I, p. 130) may be performed by this class, and shooting attacks (CR I, p. 130) are exclusive to Marksmen.\nUnlike other Warrior-type classes, the Marksman class doesn't increase Evasion, making it dangerous to get caught up in close combat.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:marksman","classType":"Warrior","weaponRestrictions":"Thrown Weapons, Bows, Crossbows, or Guns (with Artificer class) only","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"When attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nWarrior-type Class\nAll ranged attacks (see CR I, p. 130) may be performed by this class, and shooting attacks (CR I, p. 130) are exclusive to Marksmen.\nUnlike other Warrior-type classes, the Marksman class doesn't increase Evasion, making it dangerous to get caught up in close combat.\nWeapon Restrictions: Thrown Weapons, Bows, Crossbows, or Guns (with Artificer class) only\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nClass Skills: Base Accuracy (thrown and ranged weapons only)\nClass Features: When attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.\nSource: CR I, p. 88; ET, p. 23\nList of Bows\nList of Crossbows\nThrown Weapons List\nAmmunition List\nMarksman Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"55eYR0s6v27MOurs","name":"Artificer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"This caster learns Magitech. They use Magitech Spheres (magispheres) to create useful tools and effects. Artificers are the only class able to use Guns, which can deliver damage, healing, and more through the use of Bullets.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:artificer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Artificers can cast any spell from the Magitech spells list of their Artificer Class level or lower.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThis caster learns Magitech. They use Magitech Spheres (magispheres) to create useful tools and effects. Artificers are the only class able to use Guns, which can deliver damage, healing, and more through the use of Bullets.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Magitech spells, an Artificer must be able to vocalize and have a Magisphere of the correct size properly equipped. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Magitech Magic only)\nClass Features: Artificers can cast any spell from the Magitech spells list of their Artificer Class level or lower.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Artificers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Magitech), calculated as Artificer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Artificer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Artificers learn to speak, read, and write the Magitech language.\nNote: Artificer Bullet spells must be cast on bullets in a gun, either equipped or in hand. Additionally, attacks with guns are Shooting attacks and Accuracy checks are made using the Marksman class, making it important to keep similarly leveled as missing does no damage and applies no affects. Extra damage is the power of the Magitech cast on the bullet (Artificer level + Intelligence modifier).\nSource: CR I, p. 89; ET, p. 32; MA, p. 125\nMagitech Spells List\nArtificer Class Combat Feats\nGuns List\nAmmunition List"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7hgpt1uVZ15rhobf","name":"Ranger","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Like the Scout, Rangers are useful for reconnaissance and investigation, but the class' capabilities tend to be limited to natural environments.\nRangers are uniquely adept at handling and administering medicinal herbs and potions. With such efficiency, Rangers contribute greatly to the safety of themselves and their party.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:ranger","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics and Follow checks when wearing metal armor","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nLike the Scout, Rangers are useful for reconnaissance and investigation, but the class' capabilities tend to be limited to natural environments.\nRangers are uniquely adept at handling and administering medicinal herbs and potions. With such efficiency, Rangers contribute greatly to the safety of themselves and their party.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics and Follow checks when wearing metal armor\nShield Restrictions: None\nSkill Packages:\n\nTechnique: Conceal, Disable Device*, Set Trap*, First Aid\nMovement: Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics, Climb, Follow\nObservation: Track, Notice*, Listen, Danger Sense, Search*, Meteorology, Spot Trap*, Cartography, Pathology, Herbology\n\n* Natural environments only\nNote: Rangers add \"Ranger class level + Dexterity Modifier\" to herb use and \"Ranger class level + Intelligence Modifier\" to potion use.\nSource: CR I, p. 89; ET, p. 38\nHerbs, Potions, and Chemicals List\nRanger Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"8bO4sOTZcC9XPSg0","name":"Sorcerer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"This caster learns Truespeech Magic. Truespeech Magic is a magic system that can be called traditional, as their spells offer many ways to deal direct damage, and at the same time, it also has convenient spells such as lighting a magical light.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:sorcerer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Sorcerers can cast any spell from the Truespeech spells list of their Sorcerer Class level or lower.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThis caster learns Truespeech Magic. Truespeech Magic is a magic system that can be called traditional, as their spells offer many ways to deal direct damage, and at the same time, it also has convenient spells such as lighting a magical light.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Truespeech spells, a Sorcerer must be able to vocalize, move their arms freely, and have a magical implement equipped. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Truespeech Magic only)\nClass Features: Sorcerers can cast any spell from the Truespeech spells list of their Sorcerer Class level or lower.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Sorcerers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Truespeech), calculated as Sorcerer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Sorcerer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Sorcerers learn to speak, read, and write the Arcana language, which they use to cast spells.\nSource: CR I, p. 88; ET, p. 26; MA, p. 78\nTruespeech Magic Spells List\nSorcerer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ANEnu9efWspMdNTK","name":"Alchemist","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Alchemists have the strange ability to process and synthesize items out of basic materials, as well as create Evocations from magically infused cards. Their Material Cards are made of Prima Materia, the essential element of various substances.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:alchemist","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Alchemists learn one Evocation per Alchemist Class level, and gain the ability to speak and read Magitech.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nAlchemists have the strange ability to process and synthesize items out of basic materials, as well as create Evocations from magically infused cards. Their Material Cards are made of Prima Materia, the essential element of various substances.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: Alchemists must have an equipped Alchemy Kit and the correct Material Cards to create Evocations. They may not take a Full Move on the same turn as creating an Evocation.\nClass Features: Alchemists learn one Evocation per Alchemist Class level, and gain the ability to speak and read Magitech.\nSkill Packages:\n\nKnowledge: Evocation, Insight, Literature, Herbology\n\nSpecial Resource: Alchemists use the Evocation skill, which uses Alchemist level + Intelligence, an Alchemy Kit or Card Shooter, and Material Cards of various ranks (B, A, S and SS) to perform Evocations.\nSource: CR III, p. 107; ET, p. 48; MA, p. 178\nAlchemist Evocations List\nAlchemist Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"D0rCBzXmHpK1su6E","name":"Bard","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Bards play musical instruments, sing songs, and produce various supportive or hindering effects on nearby listeners. Bard Spellsongs increase Rhythm, which they can use to unleash spectacular Finales and change the tide of battle.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:bard","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Bards learn one Spellsong or Finale per Bard Class level (which can be increased with the [Additional Songs] feat). Each Bard Class level also allows them to speak, but not read, one new language.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nBards play musical instruments, sing songs, and produce various supportive or hindering effects on nearby listeners. Bard Spellsongs increase Rhythm, which they can use to unleash spectacular Finales and change the tide of battle.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: Bards must be able to play an instrument to use Spellsongs and Finales. Some Spellsongs require singing as well. They may only take a Limited Move on the same turn as using a Spellsong or Finale.\nClass Features: Bards learn one Spellsong or Finale per Bard Class level (which can be increased with the [Additional Songs] feat). Each Bard Class level also allows them to speak, but not read, one new language.\nSkill Packages:\n\nInsight Checks\nPerformance Checks\n\nSpecial Resources: Bards gain the unique statistic Bardic Power, which plays a role similar to Magic Power in Wizard-type Classes. Bardic Power is calculated as Bard Class Level + Spirit Modifier.\nBards accumulate a resource called Rhythm by playing Spellsongs. These three types of Rhythm, Uplifting (⮭), Calming (⮯), and Enchanting (♡), are used to perform Finales.\nSpellsongs and Finales have a range equal to (Bard Class Level x 10)m, centered on the Bard. In Simplified Combat, Spellsongs and Finales have a range of 2 Areas at Bard Class Level 1, and the entire battlefield for Bard Class Level 2+.\nSource: CR II, p. 100; ET, p. 44; MA, p. 163\nBard Spellsongs List\nBard Finales List\nSpecial Instruments List\nBard Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DP6kQ4biNhL4TTig","name":"Battle Dancer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The Battle Dancer class is a unique specialization within the Warrior category. Unlike other warriors, Battle Dancers eschew heavy armor and instead rely on nimble movements resembling a dance to manipulate their weapons.\nAs masters of attack, Battle Dancers employ a wide array of Combat Feats and utilize multiple attacks in combat. However, due to the class's rarity and the high casualty rate resulting from its low defense, few adventurers have truly mastered the art of the Battle Dancer.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:battle-dancer","classType":"Warrior","weaponRestrictions":"None; may also equip Wrestling weapons","armourRestrictions":"Only items marked \"Martial Artists may equip\" or \"Martial Artists only\"","shieldRestrictions":"May not equip","classFeatures":"At Level 1, Battle Dancers receive one bonus Active Combat Feat from the following list: [Decoy Attack I], [Repeated Strike I], [Aimed Attack I], [Power Strike I], [Taunting Strike I], [Lethal Strike I], [Mana Strike], [Shadow Step I] (Vagrants only), [Desperate Strike I] (Vagrants only), [Herald Strike] (Vagrants only), and [Wild Strike I] (Vagrants only). This Combat Feat only applies to the Battle Dancer Class and cannot be \"shared\" with other classes.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWarrior-type Class\nThe Battle Dancer class is a unique specialization within the Warrior category. Unlike other warriors, Battle Dancers eschew heavy armor and instead rely on nimble movements resembling a dance to manipulate their weapons.\nAs masters of attack, Battle Dancers employ a wide array of Combat Feats and utilize multiple attacks in combat. However, due to the class's rarity and the high casualty rate resulting from its low defense, few adventurers have truly mastered the art of the Battle Dancer.\nWeapon Restrictions: None; may also equip Wrestling weapons\nArmor Restrictions: Only items marked \"Martial Artists may equip\" or \"Martial Artists only\"\nShield Restrictions: May not equip\nClass Skills: Base Accuracy (melee, wrestling, and thrown weapons only), Evasion\nClass Features: At Level 1, Battle Dancers receive one bonus Active Combat Feat from the following list: [Decoy Attack I], [Repeated Strike I], [Aimed Attack I], [Power Strike I], [Taunting Strike I], [Lethal Strike I], [Mana Strike], [Shadow Step I] (Vagrants only), [Desperate Strike I] (Vagrants only), [Herald Strike] (Vagrants only), and [Wild Strike I] (Vagrants only). This Combat Feat only applies to the Battle Dancer Class and cannot be \"shared\" with other classes.\nWhen attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.\nSource: BM, p. 12; BM, p. 92\nBattle Dancer Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"E2hC4cG4rM0M8QA5","name":"Scout","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Scouts excel at reconnaissance and investigation. They have a variety of skills that benefit hiding, concealment, searching, and can sense danger and traps. Scouts also possess the Initiative skill, which is essential for your party to be the first to act in combat. However, some skills are highly penalized by wearing Metal Armor.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:scout","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics and Follow checks when wearing metal armor","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nScouts excel at reconnaissance and investigation. They have a variety of skills that benefit hiding, concealment, searching, and can sense danger and traps. Scouts also possess the Initiative skill, which is essential for your party to be the first to act in combat. However, some skills are highly penalized by wearing Metal Armor.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics and Follow checks when wearing metal armor\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: Some Scout skill package checks will incur a -4 penalty if the Scout is not carrying Scout's Tools.\nSkill Packages:\n\nTechnique: Pickpocket, Disguise, Conceal, Disable Device, Set Trap\nMovement: Initiative, Tumble, Hide, Acrobatics, Climb, Follow\nObservation: Track, Notice, Listen, Danger Sense, Search, Meteorology, Spot Trap, Cartography, Appraise\n\nSource: CR I, p. 89; ET, p. 36\nScout Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"I2fJn8czLSta3zwa","name":"Fencer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Warrior-type Combat Class\nAlthough inferior to Fighters and Martial Artists when comparing raw offense and defense, the Fencer comes with varied attacks and the potential to unleash incredible one-hit damage. The Fencer's Strength Score is halved (rounding up) to determine which Minimum Strength requirements they meet when equipping weapons, armors, and shields. However, Fencers benefit from an increased chance of generating critical damage (see CR I p. 136) with any weapon they wield.\nThe Fencer's higher critical chance comes with the potential to unleash incredible one-hit damage. As a Minor class, the Fencer's faster growth rate is another benefit when advancing alongside other classes.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:fencer","classType":"Warrior","weaponRestrictions":"1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement","armourRestrictions":"1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement","shieldRestrictions":"1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement","classFeatures":"Weapons wielded by a Fencer receive -1 to their normal Critical Threshold (minimum 8).","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nWarrior-type Combat Class\nAlthough inferior to Fighters and Martial Artists when comparing raw offense and defense, the Fencer comes with varied attacks and the potential to unleash incredible one-hit damage. The Fencer's Strength Score is halved (rounding up) to determine which Minimum Strength requirements they meet when equipping weapons, armors, and shields. However, Fencers benefit from an increased chance of generating critical damage (see CR I p. 136) with any weapon they wield.\nThe Fencer's higher critical chance comes with the potential to unleash incredible one-hit damage. As a Minor class, the Fencer's faster growth rate is another benefit when advancing alongside other classes.\nWeapon Restrictions: 1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement\nArmor Restrictions: 1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement\nShield Restrictions: 1/2 (round up) Strength Score for Minimum Strength requirement\nClass Skills: Base Accuracy (melee and thrown weapons only), Evasion\nClass Features: Weapons wielded by a Fencer receive -1 to their normal Critical Threshold (minimum 8).\nWhen attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.\nSource: CR I, p. 88; ET, p. 22\nFencer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"IASXh4am3C5mPeUI","name":"Sage","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"A Sage's strength lies in all matters where knowledge is concerned. Sages provide the Monster Knowledge skill, which identifies the characteristics of monsters, as well as how to exploit their weaknesses.\nEvery time the Sage class is advanced, a new language can be learned. Sages may learn to either speak or read from any language from the list of languages (see CR I, p. 74).","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:sage","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nA Sage's strength lies in all matters where knowledge is concerned. Sages provide the Monster Knowledge skill, which identifies the characteristics of monsters, as well as how to exploit their weaknesses.\nEvery time the Sage class is advanced, a new language can be learned. Sages may learn to either speak or read from any language from the list of languages (see CR I, p. 74).\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nSkill Packages:\n\nKnowledge: Monster Knowledge, Appraise, Cartography, Pathology, Herbology, Insight, Literature, Engineering\n\nSource: CR I, p. 89; ET, p. 40\nSage Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"OCSQ03DD0EX91mSW","name":"Tactician","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"The Tactician class inspires and motivates allies in battle, leading them to victory with their charisma, precise touch, and reputation. The main features of the Tactician class are increased Initiative and Stratagems and Maneuvers which support allies. As a Tactician, a character can lead their comrades, take the initiative, and support their allies with Stratagems when the battle begins.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:tactician","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Tacticians learn one Stratagem or Maneuver per Tactician Class level. This can be increased with the [Additional Stratagem/Maneuver] feat.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nThe Tactician class inspires and motivates allies in battle, leading them to victory with their charisma, precise touch, and reputation. The main features of the Tactician class are increased Initiative and Stratagems and Maneuvers which support allies. As a Tactician, a character can lead their comrades, take the initiative, and support their allies with Stratagems when the battle begins.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To use Stratagems and Maneuvers, the Tactician must be able to vocalize, and have a properly equipped Strategist's Insignia. Stratagems and Maneuvers can only be used in combat situations.\nClass Features: Tacticians learn one Stratagem or Maneuver per Tactician Class level. This can be increased with the [Additional Stratagem/Maneuver] feat.\nSkill Packages:\n\nInitiative check\n\nSpecial Resource: Tacticians gain a class-specific resource called Edge by using Stratagems, which they can spend to activate Maneuvers and a few powerful Stratagems.\nNote: A Tactician's Stratagems and Maneuvers affect all Allies in the area (see below) that the Tactician is aware of, has Low, Average, or High intellect, and shares at least one language. A Tactician is not affected by their own Stratagems unless noted in the Stratagem.\nTactician Commanding Area Table\n\nAdventurer Rank\nCommanding Area\n\nNone\n1 area (5m Radius)\n\nDagger\n2-3 areas (10m Radius)\n\nRapier\nAll areas (20m Radius)\n\nBroad Sword\nAll areas (30m Radius)\n\nFlamberge\nAll areas (40m Radius)\n\nSentinel\nAll areas (50m Radius)\n\nHyperion\nAll areas (100m Radius)\n\nSword of Genesis\nAll areas (200m Radius*)\n\n* add 100m for each star rank\n\nSource: MA, p. 29; MA, p. 51\nTactician Stratagems List\nTactician Maneuvers List\nTactician Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"PrS95dDCMTDiCcMo","name":"Martial Artist","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"This warrior fights with their body, punching and kicking foes, as well as other techniques. Although limited to wrestling-type weapons and severely limited in armor choice, Martial Artists automatically acquire the Passive Combat Feat [Chain Attack], which gives them the advantage of multiple attacks. The Throw wrestling weapon can be used to slam enemies into the ground, further granting the upper hand in battle.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:grappler","classType":"Warrior","weaponRestrictions":"Only Wrestling weapons","armourRestrictions":"Only items marked \"Martial Artists may equip\" or \"Martial Artists only\"","shieldRestrictions":"May not equip","classFeatures":"Martial Artists receive automatic access to the [Chain Attack] feat and the exclusive Wrestling technique Throw.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWarrior-type Class\nThis warrior fights with their body, punching and kicking foes, as well as other techniques. Although limited to wrestling-type weapons and severely limited in armor choice, Martial Artists automatically acquire the Passive Combat Feat [Chain Attack], which gives them the advantage of multiple attacks. The Throw wrestling weapon can be used to slam enemies into the ground, further granting the upper hand in battle.\nWeapon Restrictions: Only Wrestling weapons\nArmor Restrictions: Only items marked \"Martial Artists may equip\" or \"Martial Artists only\"\nShield Restrictions: May not equip\nClass Skills: Base Accuracy (wrestling weapons only), Evasion\nClass Features: Martial Artists receive automatic access to the [Chain Attack] feat and the exclusive Wrestling technique Throw.\nWhen attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.\nSource: CR I, p. 87; ET, p. 20\nWrestling Weapons List\nMartial Artist Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Rx7kqRoEujZMwfFL","name":"Rider","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Riders can control Mounts of various types and make them perform a large array of Stunts. Those PCs with Rider class levels are colloquially known as Jockeys.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:rider","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Riders learn one Stunt per Rider Class level.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nRiders can control Mounts of various types and make them perform a large array of Stunts. Those PCs with Rider class levels are colloquially known as Jockeys.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nClass Features: Riders learn one Stunt per Rider Class level.\nSkill Packages:\n\nMovement: Tumble, Riding\nKnowledge: Weakness, Cartography, Monster Knowledge (for identifying monsters only, cannot determine Weaknesses)\nFirst Aid checks\n\nBenefits Summary\n\nCan control Mounts with one hand.*\nUse a Minor Action to mount/dismount.*\nCan make Riding Checks.*\nCan raise a Mount's level to be the same as their Adventurer Level.*\nCan use Stunts.*\nCan rent Mounts from the Riders Guild (CR III p. 267).\nCan purchase equipment for Mounts and use it.\n\n*To qualify for these benefits, the character's Rider level must meet the Mount's \"Appropriate Minimum Level\".\nSee Also: Double Riding and the Mounted Unique Skill\nSource: CR III, p. 84; ET, p. 46; MA, p. 173\nRider Stunts List\nList of Mounts\nMount Items, Weapons, Armor\nRider Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Uf1jMIbW9gkkCe4r","name":"Fairy Tamer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The Fairy Tamer is a class that uses Fairy Magic. Fairies are beings born from the interference of mana with nature, and they exist everywhere in Raxia. Fairy Magic is the art of making a contract with these fairies and having them use their powers in exchange for the caster's mana.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:fairy-tamer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Fairy Tamers can cast any Basic spell, or spell matching their daily allotment of Fairy Tamer gems, from the Fairy Magic spells list of their Fairy Tamer Class level or lower. Fairy Tamers may also summon Fairies. See CR II, p. 94 for more information.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThe Fairy Tamer is a class that uses Fairy Magic. Fairies are beings born from the interference of mana with nature, and they exist everywhere in Raxia. Fairy Magic is the art of making a contract with these fairies and having them use their powers in exchange for the caster's mana.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Fairy Magic spells, a Fairy Tamer must be able to vocalize and carry Fairy Tamer's Gems of the correct color and quality. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Fairy Magic only)\nClass Features: Fairy Tamers can cast any Basic spell, or spell matching their daily allotment of Fairy Tamer gems, from the Fairy Magic spells list of their Fairy Tamer Class level or lower. Fairy Tamers may also summon Fairies. See CR II, p. 94 for more information.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Fairy Tamers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Fairy Magic), calculated as Fairy Tamer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Fairy Tamer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Fairy Tamers learn to speak the Sylvan language.\nNote: Runefolk cannot perceive fairies and therefore cannot acquire the Fairy Tamer class. Lykants cannot use Fairy Magic while in [Beast Form].\nSource: CR II, p. 94; CR III, p. 114; ET, p. 34; MA, p. 135\nFairy Magic Spells List\nFairy Tamer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WSCmVAIufvy6I1Sx","name":"Abyss Gazer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The Abyss Gazer Class uses mana to draw out supernatural phenomena that normally only occur in a Shallow Abyss and manipulate them at will. Rifts and gaps in space that lead to Shallow Abysses exist everywhere, and Abyss Gazers can draw on their power to manipulate various phenomena.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:abyss-gazer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Abyss Gazers can cast any spell from the Abyssal Magic spells list of their Abyss Gazer Class level or lower. Abyss Gazers may also enhance their spells with Enhancement Materials.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThe Abyss Gazer Class uses mana to draw out supernatural phenomena that normally only occur in a Shallow Abyss and manipulate them at will. Rifts and gaps in space that lead to Shallow Abysses exist everywhere, and Abyss Gazers can draw on their power to manipulate various phenomena.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Abyssal Magic, Abyss Gazers must be able to vocalize, move at least one arm freely enough to make a slashing motion in the air, and have an Abyssal Knife equipped. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Abyssal Magic only)\nClass Features: Abyss Gazers can cast any spell from the Abyssal Magic spells list of their Abyss Gazer Class level or lower. Abyss Gazers may also enhance their spells with Enhancement Materials.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Abyss Gazers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Abyssal), calculated as Abyss Gazer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Abyss Gazer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Abyss Gazers learn to speak the Daemonic language, which they use to cast spells.\nSource: AB p. 18\nAbyssal Magic Spells List\nAbyss Gazer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Y5w7OmDkxcBA4bMS","name":"Priest","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"This caster learns Divine Magic. Through faith, Priests heal and mitigate damage, as well as oppose Barbarous and Undead creatures. When you first become a Priest, you will choose a single deity whom you worship, and in turn they will grant you specialized, and thematic, spells.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:priest","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Priests can cast any spell from the Divine spells list of their Priest Class level or lower. Priests must also select a divinity to worship, which gives them access to unique spells.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThis caster learns Divine Magic. Through faith, Priests heal and mitigate damage, as well as oppose Barbarous and Undead creatures. When you first become a Priest, you will choose a single deity whom you worship, and in turn they will grant you specialized, and thematic, spells.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Divine Magic, a Priest must be able to vocalize. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Priests gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Divine), calculated as Priest Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Priest Level) MP.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Divine Magic only)\nClass Features: Priests can cast any spell from the Divine spells list of their Priest Class level or lower. Priests must also select a divinity to worship, which gives them access to unique spells.\nLanguages: Priests do not need to learn a specialized language to cast their spells.\nNotes: Runefolk and Tabbits cannot take the Priest class.\nIf a priest of a Major or Minor god leaves their god's area of influence, they will have to pay additional MP, before any multiplication, to cast spells, as shown below. This can be negated through establishing Shrines or Missions (CR II p. 93), or by carrying Portable Shrines or Purifying Holy Symbols.\nDivinity and Influence\n\nDivinity\nArea of Influence\nMP Cost Increase\n\nAncient God\nAll of Raxia\n-\n\nMajor God\nContinent\n+1\n\nMinor God\nRegion\n+2\n\nSource: CR I, p. 88; CR II, p. 93; ET, p. 30; MA, p. 101\nDivine Magic Spells List\nDivine Magic Spells List, Sorted by Diety\nPriest Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hLqdm7JpepasoL5z","name":"Geomancer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"The Geomancer class utilizes the power of world creation by harnessing the Qi (life force) that fills the world. They can exert various effects around them, making them the Masters of the Land.\nGeomancers' effects are called Aspects, broadly categorized into those that deal fixed damage, those that give disadvantages, those that heal, and those that give advantages.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:geomancer","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Geomancers learn one Aspect per Geomancer Class level.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nThe Geomancer class utilizes the power of world creation by harnessing the Qi (life force) that fills the world. They can exert various effects around them, making them the Masters of the Land.\nGeomancers' effects are called Aspects, broadly categorized into those that deal fixed damage, those that give disadvantages, those that heal, and those that give advantages.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To use Aspects, a Geomancer must deploy a Geograph. While the Geograph is deployed, a Geomancer can only make a Limited Move on the same turn as Aspects are dispatched.\nClass Features: Geomancers learn one Aspect per Geomancer Class level.\nSkill Packages:\n\nObservation: Search, Meteorology\n\nSpecial Resources: While a Geomancer has a Geograph deployed, they earn one point of all types of Qi every 10 seconds. The three types of Qi are Heavenly Qi, Earthly Qi, and Spirit Qi. The ultimate amount of Qi which can be stored depends on the Geograph. Gathered Qi points are then spent to create Aspects. The target of each active Aspect is determined randomly each turn.\nSource: MA, p. 18; MA, p. 49\nGeomancer Aspects List\nGeomancer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"t5xQ9lhZtBFhlOJw","name":"Daemonologist","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The Daemonologist class can wield powerful magic, summoning Daemons and utilizing their otherworldly abilities. Daemonologists can specialize in offensive spellcasting or become magic warriors. They also have the ability to summon Daemons and fight alongside them, although this is a risky endeavor. Depending on the combination, it may unleash powerful Daemons into the world of Raxia.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:daemonologist","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Daemonologists can cast any spell from the Summoning Arts spells list of their Daemonologist Class level or lower. Daemonologists can also summon Daemons with a Monster Level equal to or less than their Adventurer Level. See ML, p. 28 for more information.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThe Daemonologist class can wield powerful magic, summoning Daemons and utilizing their otherworldly abilities. Daemonologists can specialize in offensive spellcasting or become magic warriors. They also have the ability to summon Daemons and fight alongside them, although this is a risky endeavor. Depending on the combination, it may unleash powerful Daemons into the world of Raxia.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To use Summoning Arts, a Daemonologist must be able to vocalize, and must carry an Imp Seal. They may only make a Limited Move on the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Summoning Arts Magic only), Banish\nClass Features: Daemonologists can cast any spell from the Summoning Arts spells list of their Daemonologist Class level or lower. Daemonologists can also summon Daemons with a Monster Level equal to or less than their Adventurer Level. See ML, p. 28 for more information.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Daemonologists gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Summoning Arts), calculated as Daemonologist Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Daemonologist Level) MP.\nLanguages: Daemonologists learn to speak Daemonic and read Arcana.\nDaemon Summoning Procedure Table\n\nStep\nProcess\nAction, Time\nMovement\nRestriction\nCost\nNotes\n\nPreparation\nFormation of Abyss Gate\nMajor/Minor Action\n(depending on armor)\nLimited Move\nNone\n\nSummoning the Daemon\nMinor Action\nLimited Move\nMP, Summoning Sacrifices\n\nTask\nDaemon's Task\nAutomatic\nAny\nNone in principle,\nMP when canceled\n\nCleanup\nBanishment of Daemon\nBanish check\n(10 minutes)\nUnable to move\nBanish Tribute,\ndepending on the situation\nReturn of MP\n\nForced (combat)\nAny\n\nClosing the Abyss Gate\nAutomatic\nAny\nNone\n\nSource: ML, p. 28; MA, p. 55\nSummoning Arts Magic Spell List\nDaemon Monster Data\nDaemon Action Charts\nDaemonologist Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tZUQGDZhTy620aBy","name":"Bibliomancer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The Bibliomancer class is designed to revive and wield a form of magic called \"Arcane Magic,\" a secret art created and used during the Magic Civilization Period. Complex spell-casting procedures were rendered into Grimoires, and on the premise of this advanced preparation, powerful magic could be used with ease.\nBibliomancers analyze ancient Grimoires discovered in ruins and other sites, refine them for their own use, and wield them. Their effects are exactly the same as those from the Magic Civilization Period, when they were wielded by wizard-kings and nobles and became symbols of awe.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:bibliomancer","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Bibliomancers can cast any Arcane Magic spell which they have acquired and transcribed into their Grimoire. The Rank and number of spells which they can prepare at any one time is dependent on their Bibliomancer Class level.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThe Bibliomancer class is designed to revive and wield a form of magic called \"Arcane Magic,\" a secret art created and used during the Magic Civilization Period. Complex spell-casting procedures were rendered into Grimoires, and on the premise of this advanced preparation, powerful magic could be used with ease.\nBibliomancers analyze ancient Grimoires discovered in ruins and other sites, refine them for their own use, and wield them. Their effects are exactly the same as those from the Magic Civilization Period, when they were wielded by wizard-kings and nobles and became symbols of awe.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor; -2 for non-metallic armor with Minimum Strength 10+\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Arcane spells, a Bibliomancer must be able to vocalize, have their Grimoire properly equipped, and be able to trace the characters written in their Grimoire precisely with one finger. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Arcane Magic only)\nClass Features: Bibliomancers can cast any Arcane Magic spell which they have acquired and transcribed into their Grimoire. The Rank and number of spells which they can prepare at any one time is dependent on their Bibliomancer Class level.\nBibliomancer Class Spell Slot Table\n\nLevel\nRank and Number of Prepared Spell Slots\nRank of Emergency Spell Slots\n\n1\n1 x Rank 1\n1\n\n2\n2 x Rank 1\n\n3\n3 x Rank 1\n\n4\n3 x Rank 1, 1 x Rank 2\n2\n\n5\n3 x Rank 1, 2 x Rank 2\n\n6\n3 x Both Ranks 1 & 2\n\n7\n3 x Ranks 1 & 2, 1 x Rank 3\n3\n\n8\n3 x Ranks 1 & 2, 2 x Rank 3\n\n9\n3 x All Ranks 1 through 3\n\n10\n3 x Ranks 1 - 3, 1 x Rank 4\n4\n\n11\n3 x Ranks 1 - 3, 2 x Rank 4\n\n12\n3 x All Ranks 1 through 4\n\n13\n3 x Ranks 1 - 4, 1 x Rank 5\n5\n\n14\n3 x Ranks 1 - 4, 2 x Rank 5\n\n15\n3 x All Ranks 1 through 5\n\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Bibliomancers gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Arcane), calculated as Bibliomancer Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Bibliomancer Level) MP.\nLanguages: Bibliomancers learn to speak, read, and write the Arcana language.\nNotes: Unlike other magic systems, Arcane Magic does not allow automatic acquisition of spells through class level advancement. Each spell becomes castable only when the Bibliomancer obtains it through some means (for instance, purchasing it from the Guild of Arcane Manuscripts or locating it during adventures).\nWhen creating a character, players may replace \"Sorcerer\" or \"Conjurer\" Classes with the Bibliomancer Class in backgrounds where those classes exist.\nSource: TC, p. 16\nArcane Magic List (English translation is currently under embargo; please visit the Sword World - Cardia's Library Discord for more information about how to acquire embargoed translations)\nBibliomancer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uOsGtfYyfQd9he61","name":"Enhancer","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"Enhancers are a very physical class who use their body and mana to create advantages in battle. It is not a class that makes use of weapons, but uses nonmagical Techniques with associated special effects.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:enhancer","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Enhancers learn one Technique per Enhancer Class level.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nEnhancers are a very physical class who use their body and mana to create advantages in battle. It is not a class that makes use of weapons, but uses nonmagical Techniques with associated special effects.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: Enhancers must be able to breathe freely to use Techniques (vocalization is not required). They may not take a Full Move on the same turn as using a Technique. All Techniques cost a base 3MP to use, but are not magical.\nClass Features: Enhancers learn one Technique per Enhancer Class level.\nSource: CR II, p. 97; ET, p. 42; MA, p. 159\nEnhancer Techniques List\nEnhancer Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"vQuddCXFwbx9IMDX","name":"Dark Hunter","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"B","xp":0,"description":"This class focuses on \"Essence Weaving,\" a technique that harnesses life force through intense concentration to produce various effects. Practitioners of this class excel at handling thrown weapons and possess a keen ability to discern Daemons' true nature and weaknesses.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:dark-hunter","classType":"Other","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Dark Hunters learn one Essence Weaving per Dark Hunter Class level.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Minor Class\nOther-type Class\nThis class focuses on \"Essence Weaving,\" a technique that harnesses life force through intense concentration to produce various effects. Practitioners of this class excel at handling thrown weapons and possess a keen ability to discern Daemons' true nature and weaknesses.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: Some Essence Weavings are used as a Major Action. If a Dark Hunter has already taken a Full Move, they cannot use this type of Essence Weaving in the same turn.\nClass Features: Dark Hunters learn one Essence Weaving per Dark Hunter Class level.\nSkill Packages:\n\nMonster Knowledge check (Daemons only)\n\nSpecial Resource: Dark Hunters gain the unique statistic Mental Power, which plays a role similar to Magic Power in Wizard-type Classes. Mental Power is calculated as Dark Hunter Class Level + Spirit Modifier.\nSource: AB p. 28\nDark Hunter Essence Weavings List\nDark Hunter Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xYGaWZNKXDVvwg3v","name":"Fighter","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"A warrior who stands on the frontline, fighting enemies with weapons. Provided that you meet the Minimum Strength and Rank proficiency, you can wield almost every melee and thrown weapon, with no particular limitations on armor or shields.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:fighter","classType":"Warrior","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"None","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"When attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWarrior-type Class\nA warrior who stands on the frontline, fighting enemies with weapons. Provided that you meet the Minimum Strength and Rank proficiency, you can wield almost every melee and thrown weapon, with no particular limitations on armor or shields.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: None\nShield Restrictions: None\nClass Skills: Base Accuracy (melee and thrown weapons only), Evasion\nClass Features: When attacking with this Class, add the class level to the damage done as Extra Damage.\nSource: CR I, p. 87; ET, p. 18\nFighter Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xn8SQEQ15btwoydW","name":"Druid","type":"class","system":{"level":1,"category":"A","xp":0,"description":"The souls of animals and plants, or spirits, dwell in the forests and the earth. Druids communicate with these mysterious beings and manipulate magic with their help.\nDruids are a type of magician that can cast Nature Magic, specializing in attack and support spells. The attack spells summon Animal and Plant spirits and are very different from other Wizard-type classes, as they deal magical damage that cannot be resisted.","sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/class:druid","classType":"Wizard","weaponRestrictions":"None","armourRestrictions":"-4 to Spellcasting for metal armor","shieldRestrictions":"None","classFeatures":"Druids can cast any spell from the Nature spells list of their Druid Class level or lower.","skillPackages":"","rawText":"Major Class\nWizard-type Class\nThe souls of animals and plants, or spirits, dwell in the forests and the earth. Druids communicate with these mysterious beings and manipulate magic with their help.\nDruids are a type of magician that can cast Nature Magic, specializing in attack and support spells. The attack spells summon Animal and Plant spirits and are very different from other Wizard-type classes, as they deal magical damage that cannot be resisted.\nWeapon Restrictions: None\nArmor Restrictions: -4 to Spellcasting for metal armor\nShield Restrictions: None\nOther Requirements: To cast Nature Magic, Druids must be able to vocalize freely, and must hold a Staff of the Sacred Tree in one hand. They may only make a Limited Move in the same turn as casting a spell.\nClass Skills: Spellcasting (Nature Magic only)\nClass Features: Druids can cast any spell from the Nature spells list of their Druid Class level or lower.\nSpecial Resource: As a Wizard-type class, Druids gain the unique statistic Magic Power (Nature), calculated as Druid Class Level + Intelligence Modifier. They also gain (3 x Druid Level) MP.\nLanguages: Druids don't require a special language to cast their spells.\nNote: Runefolk cannot become Druids. Additionally the spells [Big Defender], [Multiple Actor], and [Plants Gift] require the target to posses a Symbol of Beneficence, which can be carried as luggage.\nSource: ML, p. 16; ML, p. 53\nNature Magic Spells List\nDruid Class Combat Feats"},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","effects":[],"sort":0}
